[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] *** Add File: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1778599132309/docs/case-studies/issue-1788/README.md
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +# Issue 1788 Case Study: Russian Telegram Translation Completion
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +Issue: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/1788
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +Pull request: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/1789
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Problem
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +Russian Telegram UI output still contained English strings in several visible flows:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `/solve` rejection reasons, for example `Disk usage is 91% (threshold: 90%)`.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `/version` section titles and labels such as `Version`, `AI Agents`, `Browsers`, `Development Tools`, `Platform`, and `Environment`.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `/limits` date/reset labels, queue labels, queue status words, and waiting reasons.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `/help` could fail Telegram Markdown parsing and only show a generic send failure.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +The issue also asked that all supported locales be checked, and that Telegram formatting failures fall back to plain text across message sends while warning the user in their detected language.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Evidence
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +Screenshots from the issue were downloaded with GitHub authentication and validated as PNG images before inspection:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- [translation-reason.png](images/translation-reason.png)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- [help-format-error.png](images/help-format-error.png)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +The source issue and PR metadata are stored in:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- [issue.json](issue.json)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- [issue-comments.json](issue-comments.json)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- [pr-1789.json](pr-1789.json)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- [related-prs.json](related-prs.json)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Fix Summary
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +The fix adds localized strings and locale-aware formatting for Telegram-facing limits, queue, version, and formatting-fallback output. It also installs a Telegram API wrapper that retries failed formatted `sendMessage` and `editMessageText` calls as plain text with a localized warning.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +Official Telegram Bot API docs describe `parse_mode` as the way to select text entity parsing modes for messages, with legacy `Markdown` still listed under formatting options: https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#formatting-options. The fallback keeps the first attempt formatted, then retries without `parse_mode` only when Telegram reports an entity parsing error.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Verification
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +Logs are stored under [test-logs](test-logs/):
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `before-fix-focused.log`: focused regressions failed before the implementation.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `after-fix-focused.log`: focused regressions passed after the implementation.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `lint.log`: `npm run lint` passed.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `npm-test.log`: `npm test` passed all 205 selected test files.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `npm-install.log`: dependency installation notes, including the local Node engine warning.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +Local verification was performed on Node v20.20.2. The package declares `node >=24.0.0`, so `npm install --ignore-scripts` was used in this workspace to avoid the local Husky prepare hook and capture a runnable test tree.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] *** Add File: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1778599132309/docs/case-studies/issue-1788/TECHNICAL_SUMMARY.md
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +# Technical Summary
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Changed Areas
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `src/telegram-safe-reply.lib.mjs`
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Adds detection for Telegram formatting/entity parsing errors.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Retries formatted replies, sends, and edits as plain text.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Prepends a localized warning before fallback text.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Provides `installTelegramFormattingFallback()` for global `sendMessage` and `editMessageText` coverage.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `src/telegram-bot.mjs`
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Installs the global formatting fallback on bot startup.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Sends `/help`, `/limits`, and `/version` through safe reply/edit paths.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Passes the detected Telegram locale into `/limits`, `/version`, queue status, and solve rejection checks.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `src/limits-i18n.lib.mjs` and `src/limits.lib.mjs`
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Localize reset dates, reset durations, queue labels, waiting reasons, and compact duration units.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Preserve English default output for existing callers.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `src/telegram-solve-queue.helpers.lib.mjs` and `src/telegram-solve-queue.lib.mjs`
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Localize resource and API waiting reasons.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Localize queue status summaries, detailed queue output, item statuses, durations, and rejection reasons.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `src/version-info.lib.mjs`
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Localizes user-facing `/version` section titles, labels, restart state, and Playwright MCP connection state.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Keeps product, runtime, language, and tool names unchanged.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `src/locales/*.lino`
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Adds the new keys for English, Russian, Chinese, and Hindi.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +  - Updates the Russian `/version` title to `Информация о версиях`.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Regression Tests
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +Focused tests were added or extended for:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Telegram formatting fallback and global send/edit wrapping.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Russian `/version` labels.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Russian `/limits` reset dates, reset durations, queue labels, and queue status words.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Russian solve queue waiting reasons and duration units.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Existing `/solve_queue` command behavior without preloaded locales.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +The final verification log shows:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `npm run lint`: passed.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `npm test`: all 205 selected test files passed.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] *** Add File: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1778599132309/docs/case-studies/issue-1788/ANALYSIS.md
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +# Analysis
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Root Causes
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +The translation gaps came from four separate patterns:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +1. Several Telegram messages called formatting functions without passing the detected Telegram locale.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +2. Queue and limits helper functions returned English strings directly instead of going through locale-aware translation helpers.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +3. `/version` mixed product names with section labels, but all labels were hard-coded in English.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +4. `/help` and some message edits called Telegram directly with Markdown. If Telegram rejected a malformed entity, the bot surfaced a send failure instead of useful content.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Important Findings
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Locale files were already available for `en`, `ru`, `zh`, and `hi`, but the queue/limits/version code paths did not consistently use them.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Telegram formatting failures are recoverable when the text content is still valid plain text. The bot only needs to remove `parse_mode` and strip Markdown syntax on retry.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Some tests import command modules without preloading locale files. User-facing text added to those modules needs an English fallback for deterministic unit tests and standalone library use.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- `src/limits.lib.mjs` was near the repository line limit. The new shared date/duration helpers were moved to `src/limits-i18n.lib.mjs` to keep lint clean.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Related Work Checked
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +The related PR search artifact is stored in [related-prs.json](related-prs.json). The most relevant prior changes were:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- #384: initial terminal and Telegram i18n for `en/ru/zh/hi`.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- #388: split UI and work language tracks.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- #676: Telegram command UI localization.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- #1447 and #1638: `/limits` output and display fixes.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +This fix extends those paths rather than replacing the existing i18n structure.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +## Telegram Formatting Reference
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +The official Telegram Bot API formatting options document the message formatting mechanism and `parse_mode` selection for HTML, MarkdownV2, and Markdown: https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#formatting-options.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +Implementation decision: keep the formatted send/edit as the primary path, then retry as plain text only for Telegram entity parsing errors such as “can't parse entities” or “can't find end of entity”. Non-formatting errors still propagate.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] *** Add File: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1778599132309/docs/case-studies/issue-1788/improvements.md
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +# Follow-up Improvements
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Convert more Telegram messages to explicit safe send/edit helpers where they still use direct Telegram calls for formatted content.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Add a small integration-style test that runs representative Telegram command output for every supported locale and checks for known English UI-label leaks.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Consider exposing locale-aware reset formatting from `limits-i18n.lib.mjs` as the only reset-time API, so new `/limits` sections do not accidentally reintroduce English date strings.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- Add a developer note for the local Node version mismatch. The package currently requires Node `>=24.0.0`, while this workspace only had Node v20.20.2 available.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] +- If Telegram formatting errors keep appearing, log a compact message fingerprint in verbose mode so repeated failures can be grouped without dumping full message bodies by default.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.922Z] [INFO] *** End Patch
