[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] *** Add File: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1778599132309/docs/case-studies/issue-1788/README.md
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +# Issue 1788 Case Study: Russian Telegram Translation Completion
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +Issue: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/1788
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +Pull request: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/1789
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +## Problem
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +Russian Telegram UI output still contained English strings in several visible flows:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `/solve` rejection reasons, for example `Disk usage is 91% (threshold: 90%)`.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `/version` section titles and labels such as `Version`, `AI Agents`, `Browsers`, `Development Tools`, `Platform`, and `Environment`.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `/limits` date/reset labels, queue labels, queue status words, and waiting reasons.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `/help` could fail Telegram Markdown parsing and only show a generic send failure.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +The issue also asked that all supported locales be checked, and that Telegram formatting failures fall back to plain text across message sends while warning the user in their detected language.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +## Evidence
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +Screenshots from the issue were downloaded with GitHub authentication and validated as PNG images before inspection:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- [translation-reason.png](images/translation-reason.png)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- [help-format-error.png](images/help-format-error.png)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +The source issue and PR metadata are stored in:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- [issue.json](issue.json)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- [issue-comments.json](issue-comments.json)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- [pr-1789.json](pr-1789.json)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- [related-prs.json](related-prs.json)
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +## Fix Summary
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +The fix adds localized strings and locale-aware formatting for Telegram-facing limits, queue, version, and formatting-fallback output. It also installs a Telegram API wrapper that retries failed formatted `sendMessage` and `editMessageText` calls as plain text with a localized warning.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +Official Telegram Bot API docs describe `parse_mode` as the way to select text entity parsing modes for messages, with legacy `Markdown` still listed under formatting options: https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#formatting-options. The fallback keeps the first attempt formatted, then retries without `parse_mode` only when Telegram reports an entity parsing error.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +## Verification
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +Logs are stored under [test-logs](test-logs/):
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `before-fix-focused.log`: focused regressions failed before the implementation.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `after-fix-focused.log`: focused regressions passed after the implementation.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `lint.log`: `npm run lint` passed.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `npm-test.log`: `npm test` passed all 205 selected test files.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `npm-install.log`: dependency installation notes, including the local Node engine warning.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +Local verification was performed on Node v20.20.2. The package declares `node >=24.0.0`, so `npm install --ignore-scripts` was used in this workspace to avoid the local Husky prepare hook and capture a runnable test tree.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] *** Add File: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1778599132309/docs/case-studies/issue-1788/TECHNICAL_SUMMARY.md
