[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +# Analysis
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +## Root Causes
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +The translation gaps came from four separate patterns:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +1. Several Telegram messages called formatting functions without passing the detected Telegram locale.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +2. Queue and limits helper functions returned English strings directly instead of going through locale-aware translation helpers.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +3. `/version` mixed product names with section labels, but all labels were hard-coded in English.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +4. `/help` and some message edits called Telegram directly with Markdown. If Telegram rejected a malformed entity, the bot surfaced a send failure instead of useful content.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +## Important Findings
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- Locale files were already available for `en`, `ru`, `zh`, and `hi`, but the queue/limits/version code paths did not consistently use them.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- Telegram formatting failures are recoverable when the text content is still valid plain text. The bot only needs to remove `parse_mode` and strip Markdown syntax on retry.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- Some tests import command modules without preloading locale files. User-facing text added to those modules needs an English fallback for deterministic unit tests and standalone library use.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- `src/limits.lib.mjs` was near the repository line limit. The new shared date/duration helpers were moved to `src/limits-i18n.lib.mjs` to keep lint clean.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +## Related Work Checked
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +The related PR search artifact is stored in [related-prs.json](related-prs.json). The most relevant prior changes were:
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- #384: initial terminal and Telegram i18n for `en/ru/zh/hi`.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- #388: split UI and work language tracks.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- #676: Telegram command UI localization.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- #1447 and #1638: `/limits` output and display fixes.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +This fix extends those paths rather than replacing the existing i18n structure.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +## Telegram Formatting Reference
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +The official Telegram Bot API formatting options document the message formatting mechanism and `parse_mode` selection for HTML, MarkdownV2, and Markdown: https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#formatting-options.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +Implementation decision: keep the formatted send/edit as the primary path, then retry as plain text only for Telegram entity parsing errors such as “can't parse entities” or “can't find end of entity”. Non-formatting errors still propagate.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] *** Add File: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1778599132309/docs/case-studies/issue-1788/improvements.md
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +# Follow-up Improvements
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- Convert more Telegram messages to explicit safe send/edit helpers where they still use direct Telegram calls for formatted content.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- Add a small integration-style test that runs representative Telegram command output for every supported locale and checks for known English UI-label leaks.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- Consider exposing locale-aware reset formatting from `limits-i18n.lib.mjs` as the only reset-time API, so new `/limits` sections do not accidentally reintroduce English date strings.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- Add a developer note for the local Node version mismatch. The package currently requires Node `>=24.0.0`, while this workspace only had Node v20.20.2 available.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] +- If Telegram formatting errors keep appearing, log a compact message fingerprint in verbose mode so repeated failures can be grouped without dumping full message bodies by default.
[2026-05-12T16:26:45.934Z] [INFO] *** End Patch
