[2026-05-12T16:37:44.919Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_416","type":"reasoning","text":"**Planning CI Workflow**\n\nI need to wait for the Continuous Integration (CI) process. Maybe I can poll every 30 seconds and won’t need a final command until it’s complete. I could update the Pull Request body to include the changeset while CI is running, but it might be best to wait and avoid commands during that period. Using `gh run watch` could block and cause a timeout, so polling with `gh run list` every 30 seconds might be more effective instead. Maintaining updates every 30 seconds sounds reasonable!\n**Executing CI Polling Command**\n\nI'm thinking of using the command `sleep 30 && gh run list ...` for polling the CI status. This approach allows me to wait 30 seconds before checking the status of the CI runs. It seems like a smooth way to manage the process without rushing things. Polling at regular intervals should keep everything in check while ensuring I’m updating any necessary information consistently. It’s a practical step to ensure I’m staying on top of the CI workflow!"}}
